{"chunk_id": "7323705e391a", "text": "Rama grants refuge to Vibhishana (Bibishana), Ravana\u2019s brother who has defected from Lanka after being insulted for advising righteousness. Descending from the sky with his companions, Vibhishana surrenders completely, offering his kingdom, life, and loyalty. Rama questions him about the military strength of the Rakshasas, and Vibhishana describes Ravana\u2019s formidable forces, including Kumbhakarna, Indrajit, and vast shape\u2011shifting armies. Despite these threats, Rama vows that Ravana cannot escape death anywhere in the cosmos and promises to install Vibhishana as king of Lanka after victory. Lakshmana ceremonially anoints Vibhishana before the monkey hosts, formalizing the alliance. The chapter ends with strategic planning: Vibhishana advises that Rama seek help from the ocean god to cross the sea to Lanka, setting the stage for the epic crossing and coming war.\nVibhishana defects from Ravana, reveals Lanka\u2019s strengths, is accepted by Rama, crowned future king, and advises seeking the ocean\u2019s help to reach Lanka.\nThemes: defection and refuge, righteous leadership, war intelligence, legitimacy of kingship, strategy to cross the ocean", "vector": [0.0006656957557424903, -0.02555999718606472, 0.011440104804933071, -0.004716832656413317, -0.013929449953138828, 0.01932983286678791, -0.014024671167135239, -0.012351504527032375, -0.023641975596547127, -0.01003899797797203, 0.013834228739142418, -0.002817516913637519, 0.009202415123581886, 0.0017955931834876537, -0.015221732668578625, -0.00450598681345582, 0.038115546107292175, -0.030470671132206917, 0.02992655150592327, -0.023288298398256302, 0.003203501459211111, -0.009603702463209629, -0.0020982595160603523, 0.009855357930064201, -0.026389777660369873, 0.00951528362929821, 0.02264895848929882, -0.021955206990242004, 0.0195882897824049, -0.006655257195234299, 0.0018023946322500706, -0.009107193909585476, 0.00822980236262083, 0.0038428413681685925, -0.02701551